{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/181857-revealing-the-supernatural-and-compromise-checks","id":181857,"title":"Revealing the supernatural and compromise checks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-27T06:38:12-07:00","id":181857,"title":"Revealing the supernatural and compromise checks","content":"So I was reading through the compromise causes, and one of them is &quot;revealing your true supernatural nature.&quot; While I agree that saying &quot;I was once an angel in service of the god machine and now I have fallen&quot; should cause a compromise check, what about other, plausible supernatural explanations? What if I were to say instead &quot;I am a witch-doctor, and can therefore take pieces of your life that are important to you in exchange for a supernatural boost to your intelligence for the next 4 years?&quot; Discovering that there is such a thing as the supernatural is usually a breaking point for mortal characters, but there's nothing in that sentence that could trace you back to being a servant of the god machine. <br /> Additionally, what about masquerading as other supernatural races? If I were to say &quot;I am a changeling, and can make bargains as such by the power of my Wyrd.&quot; would that cause a compromise, or just an angry Summer Court Troll wondering why I'm shooting my mouth off?<br /> What about masquerading as fictionalized versions of the truth? Would pretending to be an actual devil working against the power of Christ (or any of the other thousands of pantheons of demons in the world) be far enough removed from the truth? What about pretending to be an angel in the service of Christ (Or any other deity in the thousands of pantheons)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3383-notaworthyrival","name":"notaworthyrival","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:17:47-07:00","id":181918,"title":"","content":"If it is OOC for that cover, then it'd be a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Flowers of Hell covers this issue in more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:40:35-07:00","id":181944,"title":"","content":"But that's just under the Acting Out of Character provision. Is there any inherrant risk to your cover just from revealing that the supernatural exists and that you are supernatural?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3383-notaworthyrival","name":"notaworthyrival","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:55:03-07:00","id":181952,"title":"","content":"Asides from calling down the wrath of the machine-forge Heaven?<br /> <br /> Well, there's also how the person takes to finding out their friend is a supernatural fiend and all the ways that can screw with them. Still, might be safer for you to unload all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:31:16-07:00","id":181988,"title":"","content":"I guess how they take it is totally up to the storyteller, and he can treat that along the same lines as the answer to question #5 (Who think's they've got something on you, but it's all smoke and mirrors?).<br /> My main question remains, do you think it would cause a compromise roll simply for stating that you are supernatural? Rather than to a friend (where it would probably fall under the Acting out of Character clause), let's take it in the context of selling a pact to a potential pact-bound, as a way to explain how you're able to offer him the moon and the stars in exchange for his relationship with his husband.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3383-notaworthyrival","name":"notaworthyrival","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:56:09-07:00","id":182016,"title":"","content":"The answer is yes. You take a compromise roll with a -4 modifier.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER. That might be preferable to having them slowly investigate what's up with you, as each smaller revelation of your supernatural nature is it's own compromise check.<br /> <br /> In the case of a deal, it's a mixed bag. Do you really think the pactbound will continue digging, or can you lose them? If the first, safer to show them maybe. If not, just do it in cover and be all mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:15:35-07:00","id":182034,"title":"","content":"Revealing that you are <i>any kind </i>of supernatural being causes the human to reel and realise you are not whom you claim to be. Your Cover is based on the thin psychic veneer of human expectation, when those expectations are subverted - even in a misleading way - they cause a compromise roll.<br /> <br /> Flowers of Hell suggests that the storyteller apply penalties based on the information. A -4 roll would be made if you give them a key fact about you, the example they give is outright saying, &quot;I am a fallen angel of the God-Machine&quot;. While lesser facts, such as &quot;I am a fallen angel&quot; that carry other connotations, might only be a -1 or a -2. A lie, I imagine is made at either a bonus or no modifier. Either way, when your cover reels after the change to expectation you run the risk of the God-Machine noticing and He isn't so easy to fool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T12:32:58-07:00","id":182149,"title":"","content":"Thank you DesolateDolly and ArcaneArts<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3383-notaworthyrival","name":"notaworthyrival","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:14:58-07:00","id":182179,"title":"","content":"You're most welcome, glad to help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}